# .ctsignore — gitignore-syntax paths that `cts-sync.sh update` will never touch.
# Use for: customized CTS files, pruned CTS files (prevents re-adding them),
# and project-only additions placed under payload directories.
#
# Two-layer model (migrated 2026-07-23): former whole-file customizations
# (AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, rules/{code-style,migrations-queue,testing,
# validation-authorization,workflow}.md, .claude/agents/{reviewer,tester,
# queue-specialist}.md, .claude/settings.json) now live as override files
# instead — AGENTS.local.md, CLAUDE.local.md, rules/local/*.md,
# .claude/agents-local/*.md. Those upstream paths are no longer ignored here
# and receive plain CTS overwrites, with the overrides layered on top per the
# lex-specialis convention. .claude/settings.json is jq deep-merged from
# .cts/settings.cts.json by the sync engine itself — never ignored.

# pruned — HPW has no frontend/UI; re-add from CTS if a UI ever appears
.claude/agents/vue-developer.md
.claude/agents/react-developer.md
.claude/agents/angular-developer.md
.claude/skills/vue-expert/
.claude/skills/react-expert/
.claude/skills/angular-expert/

# customized — HPW is pure Jest (jest.config.ts/.cts in every app/lib,
# jest/ts-jest/@swc/jest deps, zero vitest in package.json). No lex-specialis
# override mechanism exists for skills (unlike rules/** and .claude/agents/**),
# so this remains a whole-file fork. Candidate for upstream contribution as a
# wider Vitest-or-Jest skill (or split into two) — not yet done, see
# docs/CLAUDE_TS_CHANGELOG.md.
.claude/skills/vitest-testing/

# customized — project-specific additions with no lex-specialis override
# mechanism (plain payload files, not rules/** or .claude/agents/**). The
# 2026-07-23 first sync under the new engine overwrote both of these before
# this .ctsignore entry existed (no prior manifest baseline to detect drift
# against) — content was manually restored from git history afterward.
/.prettierignore
/docs/METRICS.md
